1
00:00:00,640 --> 00:00:03,690
A few days have passed since the France match.

2
00:00:07,900 --> 00:00:13,610
Japan's 11 players are training hard for the final match against Germany.

3
00:00:16,120 --> 00:00:22,370
At midnight, Tsubasa and his teammates fell asleep after training.

4
00:00:22,750 --> 00:00:25,290
Except for one person.

5
00:00:25,620 --> 00:00:29,380
Technique: Front post header, going for a direct goal.

6
00:00:32,880 --> 00:00:35,880
~Japan - Nankatsu~

7
00:00:34,930 --> 00:00:37,680
I hope they win the final.

8
00:00:37,760 --> 00:00:39,100
Yes.

9
00:00:44,480 --> 00:00:47,190
Hey, you can't rest now.

10
00:00:47,270 --> 00:00:51,070
Yeah, but it's the final tonight.

11
00:00:51,150 --> 00:00:53,530
We want to watch the live broadcast.

12
00:00:53,610 --> 00:00:56,780
If we don't rest now, we'll collapse from exhaustion.

13
00:00:57,240 --> 00:00:59,120
Don't make excuses!

14
00:01:01,580 --> 00:01:05,040
This year's U-15s are really good.

15
00:01:07,540 --> 00:01:12,800
Japan youth are playing in the final against Germany this evening!

16
00:01:07,920 --> 00:01:11,840
I'm sure this Japan team will succeed.

17
00:01:11,920 --> 00:01:14,090
The final is this evening, right?

18
00:01:12,840 --> 00:01:18,300
Japan youth are playing in the final against Germany this evening!

19
00:01:14,210 --> 00:01:18,300
I support these professionals, I'll definitely watch the match.

20
00:01:18,890 --> 00:01:23,100
Kanda, you and Ozora Tsubasa go to the same high school, right?

21
00:01:23,180 --> 00:01:25,390
What's he like? Have you spoken to him?

22
00:01:27,730 --> 00:01:30,060
Hey, what's wrong all of a sudden?

23
00:01:31,690 --> 00:01:33,320
No, nothing.

24
00:01:49,380 --> 00:01:54,300
CAPTAIN TSUBASA: JUNIOR YOUTH ARC

25
00:03:28,930 --> 00:03:33,440
Nakazawa Sanae

26
00:03:29,590 --> 00:03:33,260
Today is the final! We're all supporting you.

27
00:03:40,440 --> 00:03:42,950
My dad is calling.

28
00:03:44,230 --> 00:03:45,950
Dad, good morning.

29
00:03:46,440 --> 00:03:50,150
Good morning Taro, so the final is today.

30
00:03:50,230 --> 00:03:52,960
Yes, it starts at 3 o'clock.

31
00:03:53,400 --> 00:03:55,960
I will definitely come and support you.

32
00:03:56,200 --> 00:03:59,460
Thanks Dad, I know we will win.

33
00:04:00,700 --> 00:04:02,220
The championship is ours!

34
00:04:03,580 --> 00:04:08,670
As we predicted, it looks like Wakashimazu won't be able to play today.

35
00:04:09,380 --> 00:04:10,250
I see.

36
00:04:10,590 --> 00:04:15,730
And Misugi and the Tachibana brothers are not in condition to play.

37
00:04:16,180 --> 00:04:21,240
Hyuga and Izawa's injuries from the France match haven't healed.

38
00:04:21,680 --> 00:04:25,980
In this situation, we have a tough task in the final.

39
00:04:26,060 --> 00:04:29,100
Oh, good morning, Katagiri-kun.

40
00:04:29,150 --> 00:04:30,560
Good morning.

41
00:04:30,610 --> 00:04:36,630
Sorry for interrupting, I'm worried about the team's current situation.

42
00:04:37,150 --> 00:04:40,750
As you heard, the situation is bad.

43
00:04:41,620 --> 00:04:43,910
Who will you put as goalkeeper?

44
00:04:52,090 --> 00:04:53,520
Genzo.

45
00:04:55,510 --> 00:04:57,590
Sugitomo-kun, what is your opinion?

46
00:04:57,800 --> 00:05:02,280
Yes, this match is too heavy for Morizaki.

47
00:05:11,980 --> 00:05:14,540
Alright, let's start the meeting.

48
00:05:15,030 --> 00:05:16,650
It's almost time.

49
00:05:16,740 --> 00:05:19,040
Time to settle the score with Germany.

50
00:05:19,700 --> 00:05:23,170
And this final couldn't be better.

51
00:05:23,830 --> 00:05:24,670
Coach!

52
00:05:27,250 --> 00:05:29,680
Genzo, you're not normally late.

53
00:05:30,290 --> 00:05:31,810
It's finally finished.

54
00:05:34,670 --> 00:05:38,060
What's this? This...

55
00:05:38,720 --> 00:05:41,510
These are special information.

56
00:05:41,640 --> 00:05:44,820
About our opponent today, the German team.

57
00:05:45,560 --> 00:05:47,450
But why did you do such a thing?

58
00:05:48,270 --> 00:05:49,450
I did it to win.

59
00:05:50,060 --> 00:05:52,270
Check your phones, I've just sent it to all of you now.

60
00:05:57,360 --> 00:05:58,360
You're right.

61
00:05:58,490 --> 00:06:00,830
You sent it now.

62
00:06:00,830 --> 00:06:01,700
From Wakabayashi to Japan Youth Team

63
00:06:01,280 --> 00:06:05,830
This is a summary of the players you will mark today.

64
00:06:01,780 --> 00:06:02,660
Number 12: Manfred Margas - Forward

65
00:06:02,700 --> 00:06:04,620
Strengths: Direct header thanks to his tall height.

66
00:06:04,700 --> 00:06:05,580
Number 11: Karl Heinz Schneider - Forward

67
00:06:05,620 --> 00:06:07,540
Strengths: Fire Shot, a forward unmatched in speed, technique, and power.

68
00:06:05,910 --> 00:06:08,160
Strengths and weaknesses and quirks during the game.

69
00:06:07,620 --> 00:06:10,340
Number 10: Franz Schester - Midfielder, when he tries to get past you...

70
00:06:08,500 --> 00:06:10,340
You can check their play from clips.

71
00:06:10,750 --> 00:06:12,170
Great.

72
00:06:12,210 --> 00:06:14,130
Very detailed.

73
00:06:14,590 --> 00:06:16,850
You even wrote about the substitutes.

74
00:06:17,380 --> 00:06:19,800
I collected these piece by piece before the tournament and finally finished it.

75
00:06:19,880 --> 00:06:21,970
Schneider and Kaltz were my teammates.

76
00:06:22,430 --> 00:06:25,010
And I played against Schester and Margas.

77
00:06:25,100 --> 00:06:28,770
In my opinion, this information is accurate.

78
00:06:29,310 --> 00:06:31,870
You don't need to memorize every player's information.

79
00:06:32,520 --> 00:06:35,940
Still, I recommend you learn the information of the player you will mark.

80
00:06:36,230 --> 00:06:39,230
Okay!

81
00:06:39,280 --> 00:06:41,570
Coach, please continue.

82
00:06:44,200 --> 00:06:47,330
Yes, thank you Genzo.

83
00:06:47,370 --> 00:06:49,880
You're welcome.

84
00:06:50,450 --> 00:06:51,250
You're welcome.

85
00:06:52,210 --> 00:06:54,380
I know I said this is a meeting.

86
00:06:54,420 --> 00:06:58,090
But at this stage, I really don't have much to say.

87
00:06:58,130 --> 00:07:02,510
Just keep fighting hard, that's all.

88
00:07:02,590 --> 00:07:03,400
Yes, coach.

89
00:07:04,260 --> 00:07:07,030
Now I'm announcing the main squad.

90
00:07:08,890 --> 00:07:11,020
We're playing with two forwards.

91
00:07:11,060 --> 00:07:12,350
Hyuga on the left.

92
00:07:12,480 --> 00:07:13,270
Yes.

93
00:07:13,350 --> 00:07:14,690
Nitta on the right.

94
00:07:14,730 --> 00:07:16,040
Yes.

95
00:07:16,400 --> 00:07:19,160
- Midfielder, Tsubasa... - Yes.

96
00:07:19,360 --> 00:07:20,910
- and Misaki... - Yes.

97
00:07:21,110 --> 00:07:22,860
- Sano... - Yes.

98
00:07:22,990 --> 00:07:24,420
- Sawada... - Yes.

99
00:07:24,700 --> 00:07:27,070
- In defense, Matsuyama... - Yes.

100
00:07:27,120 --> 00:07:28,870
- Ishizaki... - Yes!

101
00:07:28,950 --> 00:07:30,420
- Jito... - Yes.

102
00:07:30,620 --> 00:07:31,790
Soda.

103
00:07:32,370 --> 00:07:33,460
Coach!

104
00:07:36,130 --> 00:07:41,440
They accepted our objection and removed the second yellow card.

105
00:07:43,260 --> 00:07:45,180
Thank you very much!

106
00:07:47,340 --> 00:07:49,140
I'm happy for you, Soda.

107
00:07:49,220 --> 00:07:52,220
I knew we would play together in the final.

108
00:07:52,350 --> 00:07:54,950
Guys, thank you.

109
00:07:55,390 --> 00:07:56,950
Let's continue.

110
00:07:58,270 --> 00:08:00,700
Yes, one person remains.

111
00:08:01,530 --> 00:08:02,960
For goalkeeper.

112
00:08:09,370 --> 00:08:10,960
Genzo Wakabayashi.

113
00:08:13,500 --> 00:08:14,710
Wakabayashi-kun!

114
00:08:14,750 --> 00:08:15,830
Wakabayashi!

115
00:08:15,960 --> 00:08:17,970
Finally, it's Wakabayashi's turn.

116
00:08:19,380 --> 00:08:22,100
Coach! This match...

117
00:08:25,010 --> 00:08:29,390
I haven't trained and coordinated with the defenders.

118
00:08:29,470 --> 00:08:31,930
And I... guys...

119
00:08:32,060 --> 00:08:34,110
Wakabayashi-san, there is no one else but you.

120
00:08:34,810 --> 00:08:41,120
Wakashimazu can't play, so only you can protect our goal today.

121
00:08:41,650 --> 00:08:43,120
Morizaki.

122
00:08:43,900 --> 00:08:46,030
That's right, Wakabayashi.

123
00:08:46,200 --> 00:08:50,120
You are the only one we can trust for Japan's goal.

124
00:08:50,160 --> 00:08:51,130
Hyuga.

125
00:08:51,660 --> 00:08:56,290
What you have said and done so far has upset some of us, including me, and no one thought well of you.

126
00:08:56,500 --> 00:08:59,640
But...

127
00:09:01,380 --> 00:09:02,840
But...

128
00:09:02,880 --> 00:09:05,390
When you step onto the field, none of this matters.

129
00:09:07,470 --> 00:09:12,600
Just show your effort and don't harm us.

130
00:09:12,680 --> 00:09:14,900
And if we can give all our focus to winning, we can play real team play.

131
00:09:15,180 --> 00:09:19,910
Actually, I couldn't stand Tsubasa.

132
00:09:20,400 --> 00:09:25,910
But on the same team, he doesn't betray my trust.

133
00:09:26,530 --> 00:09:31,170
And if this helps us win, I'll be happy to pass the ball to Tsubasa.

134
00:09:31,990 --> 00:09:37,790
Hyuga-kun.

135
00:09:38,500 --> 00:09:39,680
Football.

136
00:09:40,670 --> 00:09:41,930
That's how football is, isn't it, Wakabayashi?

137
00:09:42,460 --> 00:09:45,430
Hyuga.

138
00:09:46,340 --> 00:09:47,810
Also.

139
00:09:48,510 --> 00:09:53,350
And also, I heard the conversation between you and Tsubasa in Hamburg.

140
00:09:55,760 --> 00:10:00,940
You deliberately played the bad guy role to strengthen us.

141
00:10:02,350 --> 00:10:07,580
From the first day of the tournament, you provoked us, you punched me...

142
00:10:08,530 --> 00:10:10,320
And you sacrificed yourself.

143
00:10:10,450 --> 00:10:16,080
For the strengthening of our Japan team!

144
00:10:17,620 --> 00:10:21,220
Hey, is what Hyuga said true?

145
00:10:23,630 --> 00:10:25,720
Yes, it's true.

146
00:10:26,130 --> 00:10:28,130
You didn't tell us anything.

147
00:10:28,800 --> 00:10:31,480
But that's you, Wakabayashi-san.

148
00:10:33,140 --> 00:10:34,980
I'm sorry about that.

149
00:10:35,600 --> 00:10:38,740
Really, your actions were very hurtful.

150
00:10:39,310 --> 00:10:40,810
You know, Wakabayashi.

151
00:10:40,930 --> 00:10:45,490
Thanks to you, we improved and became strong in a short time.

152
00:10:47,320 --> 00:10:48,530
So, what will you do?

153
00:10:48,570 --> 00:10:52,660
Are you thinking of withdrawing from this tournament?

154
00:10:52,910 --> 00:10:57,010
Didn't you prepare this report?

155
00:10:57,330 --> 00:11:00,160
Wakabayashi, there is no one else for the goal but you.

156
00:11:00,250 --> 00:11:03,920
We want to see your defense in our goal, Wakabayashi-san.

157
00:11:03,960 --> 00:11:06,170
Play, Wakabayashi-san.

158
00:11:06,250 --> 00:11:07,210
Play.

159
00:11:07,340 --> 00:11:09,770
We've come this far, it can't be without you playing.

160
00:11:13,680 --> 00:11:15,770
Please, Wakabayashi.

161
00:11:16,140 --> 00:11:17,600
Wakashimazu.

162
00:11:18,640 --> 00:11:22,350
Wakabayashi-kun, protect Japan's goal.

163
00:11:25,150 --> 00:11:26,360
Genzo.

164
00:11:33,820 --> 00:11:34,790
Okay.

165
00:11:35,320 --> 00:11:37,300
I'll do it! I'll play!

166
00:11:37,490 --> 00:11:38,370
Hooray!

167
00:11:38,450 --> 00:11:39,700
That's the right decision.

168
00:11:39,830 --> 00:11:41,910
We were waiting for those words.

169
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:43,960
As long as I play, we will win!

170
00:11:44,040 --> 00:11:46,310
We will win this tournament, guys!

171
00:11:46,460 --> 00:11:49,340
Let's do this!

172
00:11:49,380 --> 00:11:50,920
I trust you, guys.

173
00:11:51,050 --> 00:11:53,310
We are all supporting you.

174
00:11:59,300 --> 00:12:02,450
Let's do this, Captain Tsubasa.

175
00:12:02,980 --> 00:12:05,450
Yes, Wakabayashi-kun.

176
00:12:06,060 --> 00:12:10,770
And now, the Japan team is reunited.

177
00:12:11,780 --> 00:12:16,070
Now we go into the final match with the strongest possible squad.

178
00:12:16,450 --> 00:12:18,450
CAPTAIN TSUBASA: JUNIOR YOUTH ARC

179
00:12:16,660 --> 00:12:19,370
Without regret.

180
00:12:24,810 --> 00:12:26,980
Born: December 7, Height: 170 cm, Weight: 63 kg, Blood Type: O

181
00:12:40,610 --> 00:12:42,320
What's wrong, Schneider?

182
00:12:42,370 --> 00:12:44,030
Nothing.

183
00:12:44,080 --> 00:12:46,540
It's almost time, let's go.

184
00:12:46,620 --> 00:12:47,500
Okay.

185
00:12:48,580 --> 00:12:55,000
Father, mother, Marie... will they come to the match today?

186
00:13:07,220 --> 00:13:08,770
Hello, Schneider.

187
00:13:09,850 --> 00:13:11,270
Felster.

188
00:13:12,520 --> 00:13:15,150
Aren't you going to go support your son?

189
00:13:16,360 --> 00:13:20,400
What is the busy Munich coach doing here?

190
00:13:20,700 --> 00:13:24,660
I considered myself lucky thinking I might see you here.

191
00:13:25,330 --> 00:13:26,870
Are you implying something?

192
00:13:26,950 --> 00:13:28,290
Implying?

193
00:13:28,620 --> 00:13:29,710
Yes.

194
00:13:31,460 --> 00:13:34,000
I don't have to go to the port anymore.

195
00:13:34,380 --> 00:13:35,880
Did you know?

196
00:13:40,220 --> 00:13:41,260
A few times...

197
00:13:42,220 --> 00:13:44,390
I saw you there a few times.

198
00:13:45,470 --> 00:13:47,890
I don't need help.

199
00:13:48,310 --> 00:13:50,980
Don't be so grumpy.

200
00:13:51,060 --> 00:13:55,860
Your Hamburg and my Munich are good rivals.

201
00:13:57,150 --> 00:13:58,860
Do you remember those good days?

202
00:13:59,530 --> 00:14:03,610
Listen, I know what happened two years ago.

203
00:14:04,160 --> 00:14:10,160
When you were an assistant coach in Hamburg, you had a problem with star player Schmidt.

204
00:14:11,830 --> 00:14:16,090
Newspapers wrote that you couldn't get along.

205
00:14:16,880 --> 00:14:21,010
And when Coach Madorov fell ill,

206
00:14:21,050 --> 00:14:25,890
you became the interim coach and everything started then.

207
00:14:26,100 --> 00:14:30,310
You removed Schmidt from the main squad.

208
00:14:31,020 --> 00:14:33,440
That interim coach is useless!

209
00:14:33,600 --> 00:14:36,520
Even if you beg, I will never play.

210
00:14:37,110 --> 00:14:39,610
Then a storm broke out in the media.

211
00:14:40,360 --> 00:14:45,910
Public opinion and the team's poor performance,

212
00:14:46,200 --> 00:14:49,790
caused the Hamburg owner to side with Schmidt.

213
00:14:49,950 --> 00:14:53,910
And they fired you and Madorov.

214
00:14:54,790 --> 00:14:58,340
And when Schmidt returned, he showed a great game.

215
00:14:58,710 --> 00:15:04,630
And thanks to him, Hamburg rose from tenth place to third.

216
00:15:06,930 --> 00:15:09,640
I'm sure it was also hard for Karl at that time.

217
00:15:13,220 --> 00:15:15,640
Hey, you're the son of that loser coach!

218
00:15:15,690 --> 00:15:18,310
They kicked your father out.

219
00:15:21,190 --> 00:15:23,530
But Karl didn't fall into despair.

220
00:15:24,190 --> 00:15:26,660
Karl continued his football.

221
00:15:26,700 --> 00:15:29,580
And he shone dazzlingly in the Hamburg youth team.

222
00:15:30,200 --> 00:15:34,000
And now he's the captain of the German youth team.

223
00:15:34,080 --> 00:15:36,790
They even call him the Young Emperor.

224
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:40,000
Karl is a strong kid.

225
00:15:40,090 --> 00:15:44,880
Didn't you teach Karl Heinz Schneider everything he knows about football?

226
00:15:46,800 --> 00:15:50,100
Also, what do you think about Schmidt this season?

227
00:15:50,180 --> 00:15:53,970
Right now he's holding everyone back.

228
00:15:54,770 --> 00:15:57,690
Lack of endurance, monotonous play...

229
00:15:58,230 --> 00:16:01,610
You knew this two years ago.

230
00:16:03,530 --> 00:16:07,400
Did you know that Karl came to my Munich team?

231
00:16:07,950 --> 00:16:08,910
Yes.

232
00:16:09,030 --> 00:16:12,370
I asked the club to send him.

233
00:16:13,790 --> 00:16:19,250
I want to play him in my great team next season.

234
00:16:22,880 --> 00:16:23,750
I see.

235
00:16:24,090 --> 00:16:27,680
And now, I've also come to win his father.

236
00:16:31,510 --> 00:16:35,140
Not for myself, but for Karl.

237
00:16:35,270 --> 00:16:38,440
Will you be my right hand and help me as coach, Schneider?

238
00:16:41,020 --> 00:16:43,570
Are you kidding, Felster?

239
00:16:43,610 --> 00:16:47,030
Why would I kid? Do you think I would joke about such a thing?

240
00:16:51,530 --> 00:16:55,790
Then can we go? Shall we go watch your son's match?

241
00:17:00,540 --> 00:17:04,550
This is the unforgettable first International Youth Tournament.

242
00:17:04,590 --> 00:17:08,290
And now it's the last day, the final day.

243
00:17:08,720 --> 00:17:13,390
Our finalist Germany hasn't lost yet.

244
00:17:13,470 --> 00:17:17,560
And they are one of the absolute championship favorites of the tournament.

245
00:17:18,350 --> 00:17:20,640
And there is Japan,

246
00:17:20,690 --> 00:17:24,060
who managed to beat Italy, Argentina, and host France

247
00:17:24,060 --> 00:17:27,740
by narrow margins.

248
00:17:27,780 --> 00:17:31,450
Even though all those teams were considered championship candidates.

249
00:17:34,070 --> 00:17:37,580
Ozora

250
00:17:34,660 --> 00:17:37,580
Which team will win?

251
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:41,580
The German youth led by the Young Emperor,

252
00:17:41,580 --> 00:17:44,830
The match is starting - Live from France

253
00:17:41,830 --> 00:17:43,210
Karl Heinz Schneider?

254
00:17:45,630 --> 00:17:47,090
Tsubasa-senpai.

255
00:17:47,090 --> 00:17:52,090
The match is starting - Live from France

256
00:17:47,300 --> 00:17:52,090
Or the Japan youth team led by the Japanese genius footballer,

257
00:17:52,300 --> 00:17:54,600
Ozora Tsubasa?

258
00:17:56,640 --> 00:18:00,480
Alright Tsubasa, it's time to spread your wings on the world stage.

259
00:18:00,680 --> 00:18:05,610
The moment to write a new page in Japanese football history is approaching.

260
00:18:06,610 --> 00:18:09,020
From a helicopter above the stadium,

261
00:18:09,060 --> 00:18:11,570
parachutists jump and display the flags of Japan, Germany

262
00:18:11,700 --> 00:18:16,570
and host France in the sky.

263
00:18:17,450 --> 00:18:19,080
Here is the final.

264
00:18:21,040 --> 00:18:23,750
And we have fireworks and an air show!

265
00:18:23,870 --> 00:18:27,090
They've prepared a wonderful show for the final.

266
